  "enhanced_information": "The patient presents with primary amenorrhea, normal breast development indicating estrogen presence, and coarse pubic and axillary hair suggesting androgen activity. The pelvic examination reveals a blind vaginal pouch and ultrasonography shows normal ovaries and an atretic uterus, indicating a failure of Müllerian duct development. This aligns with the diagnosis of agenesis of the paramesonephric duct (Müllerian agenesis), which is the most likely underlying cause of her symptoms. Other options, such as deficiency of 5-alpha reductase, end-organ insensitivity to androgens, monosomy of sex chromosomes, and deficiency of 17-alpha-hydroxylase, do not fit the clinical picture as they would present with different findings or hormonal profiles."
